  "years": "1996-2001",
  "notes": "Sport 1100, V10 Centauro and Daytona RS. This controller uses Marelli's pre-KWP echoed one-byte diagnostic protocol, not ISO 14230 frames. The physical initialization and register layout are corroborated by a field capture/open implementation for the IAW 1.6M family, the published Marelli 16F protocol, IAW Scan 2's independent 16F implementation, and ScanST's tested Moto Guzzi 16M support. Temperature conversion differs between the 16F publication (-40 C) and the recovered 1.6M implementation (-55 C), so the workstation deliberately exposes those channels as raw counts. Active-test bytes, clear-errors and reset bytes are known but intentionally unavailable: they are ECU-timed single-byte commands and do not fit the workstation's explicit on/off safety contract.",
